## 9. WEBSITE DATA MODEL

Website content must not be hard-coded per customer.

Website variation is produced from:

- structured content
- media
- theme tokens
- selected components
- component order
- component variant
- package feature flags
- language
- country configuration

Core hierarchy:

Website
→ Pages
→ Page Sections
→ Component Version
→ Structured Content
→ Style Configuration

Publishing model:

Draft Configuration
→ Immutable Website Version
→ QA
→ Customer Approval
→ Deployment
→ Published Version

Rules:

- Published versions are immutable
- Editing a published website creates a new draft/version
- Rollback must point to a previously successful version
- Component deprecation must not break existing websites
- Published component versions must remain renderable

