## 15. DEVELOPMENT PRINCIPLES

- Domain-first
- Modular monolith for MVP
- Separate modules clearly enough for future service extraction
- Server-side authorization
- Tenant isolation
- Immutable published records
- Version every publishable artifact
- Prefer configuration over customer-specific code
- Human review required for AI output
- Audit sensitive operations
- Idempotent financial and deployment operations
- Use event-driven jobs for slow processes
- Avoid direct module-to-module database writes
- Use service interfaces and domain events
- Do not place business logic in UI components
- Do not expose database models directly through APIs
- Validate all external input
- Use explicit state transitions
- Use soft delete only where business recovery is required
- Financial records should not be physically deleted

---

## 16. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

Mandatory:

- Password hashing using modern algorithm
- MFA for privileged roles
- Secure session and refresh token rotation
- CSRF protection where cookie authentication is used
- Rate limiting
- Brute-force protection
- Row-level tenant checks
- Signed upload URLs
- Malware/file validation for uploads
- Webhook signature validation
- Sensitive data encryption
- Audit logs for:
  - login risk events
  - role changes
  - user suspension
  - quotation approval
  - contract activation
  - subscription changes
  - invoice issue
  - refund
  - readiness override
  - QA override
  - website approval
  - deployment
  - rollback
  - commission approval
  - payout

Separation of duties:

- Quotation requester cannot approve own exception
- Invoice creator should not be sole issuer/void approver
- Refund requester cannot approve own refund
- Website implementer cannot approve own QA
- Customer editor and customer approver should be separate where possible
- Commission rule editor cannot approve payout
- Payout approver cannot record the same payout

---

## 17. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

Performance:

- Normal API p95 target below 500 ms
- Dashboard queries may use cached aggregates
- Large reports should run asynchronously
- Media uploads must use presigned URLs
- Website rendering should use static generation, ISR or CDN caching

Availability:

- Production platform target: 99.9%
- Public customer websites must degrade independently from back-office issues

Scalability:

- Multi-country configuration
- Horizontal application scaling
- Background job workers
- Queue-based AI, deployment and notification processing

Reliability:

- Retry external integrations safely
- Use idempotency for duplicate requests
- Deployment rollback supported
- Payment webhook event deduplication

Maintainability:

- Typed APIs
- OpenAPI source of truth
- Automated tests
- Migration scripts
- Structured modules
- Feature flags

Accessibility:

- WCAG 2.1 AA target
- Keyboard navigation
- Semantic HTML
- Sufficient contrast
- Form error association

Localization:

- Thai and English first
- Country-specific currency, timezone, tax and date formats
- Website content may support multiple languages

