## 19. BUSINESS RULES

BR-001: Website belongs to exactly one Tenant.

BR-002: Tenant requires an active Subscription to publish.

BR-003: Package price and features must be snapshotted when Subscription starts.

BR-004: Missing critical intake fields block Production.

BR-005: Critical QA issues block customer approval and deployment.

BR-006: Approved Website Version is locked.

BR-007: Feedback after approval creates a new Ticket or revision cycle.

BR-008: Support quota resets by billing period.

BR-009: AI-generated content requires human approval.

BR-010: Deprecated Component cannot be used for new websites but must render old versions.

BR-011: Partner can only access attributed customers.

BR-012: Past Due must pass grace period before suspension.

BR-013: Published configuration cannot be edited directly.

BR-014: Publish, rollback, permission and financial changes require Audit Log.

BR-015: Customer transactional data must be tenant-scoped.

BR-016: Signed Contract versions are immutable.

BR-017: Issued Invoices cannot be edited; correction uses void or credit process.

BR-018: Payment event must be deduplicated by provider event ID.

BR-019: Customer approval must reference an exact Website Version.

BR-020: Production deployment requires:
- active subscription
- passed QA
- customer approval
- valid domain or temporary domain
- valid deployable version

BR-021: Rollback requires reason and audit log.

BR-022: Commission becomes payable only after qualifying invoice is paid.

BR-023: Tenant suspension must not delete data.

BR-024: Customer export and termination rules follow contract ownership terms.

BR-025: Country configuration controls pricing, tax, currency, locale and available packages.

---

## 20. TESTING STRATEGY

Required test layers:

- Unit tests
- Domain state transition tests
- Permission tests
- Tenant isolation tests
- API contract tests
- Integration tests
- Database migration tests
- Payment webhook tests
- Idempotency tests
- Website rendering snapshot tests
- End-to-end tests
- UAT

Critical E2E scenarios:

1. Lead → Quotation → Contract → Subscription
2. Subscription → Onboarding → Readiness → Production
3. Production → QA → Review → Approval → Deployment
4. Invoice → Payment → Subscription activation
5. Past due → Grace period → Suspension → Reactivation
6. Ticket → Quota consumption → Completion
7. Out-of-scope ticket → Estimate → Approval → Billing
8. Partner lead → Customer → Paid invoice → Commission
9. Website publish → New revision → Rollback
10. Cross-tenant unauthorized access is rejected

---

## 21. DEFINITION OF DONE

A feature is complete only when:

- Acceptance criteria are met
- Permission code is defined
- Scope rule is implemented
- Validation is implemented
- API documentation is updated
- Audit behavior is defined
- Error handling is implemented
- Unit and integration tests pass
- Tenant isolation is tested
- UI supports loading, empty, error and success states
- Accessibility basics are checked
- Migration is included when data changes
- Monitoring/logging is added for critical flow
- No secret or tenant data is exposed

