## 23. AGENT IMPLEMENTATION RULES

When generating or modifying code:

1. Read this file before making architecture decisions.
2. Preserve multi-tenant isolation.
3. Do not add customer-specific hard-coded UI or logic.
4. Use package, blueprint, component and configuration models.
5. Use explicit permission codes.
6. Add server-side scope checks.
7. Use state transition services instead of direct status updates.
8. Keep published artifacts immutable.
9. Add audit events for critical actions.
10. Add idempotency to financial and deployment writes.
11. Reuse shared schemas and error types.
12. Update OpenAPI when API behavior changes.
13. Update migrations and data dictionary when database structure changes.
14. Add tests for authorization, state transition and tenant isolation.
15. Prefer small, reviewable changes.
16. Do not silently change business rules.
17. Mark unresolved decisions clearly as TODO or ADR.
18. Do not expose internal IDs in public token-based pages unless necessary.
19. Avoid destructive database operations.
20. Never bypass QA or approval without an explicit override flow.

